@NODE intro "Overview - Introduction"
@TOC contents
@{" 1     Overview                      " LINK intro}
@{" 1.1   Introduction                  " LINK intro}

Thank you very much for purchasing the AmiGUS mini soundcard. It was
designed to enable high-resolution audio playback on your Amiga
computer. All audio processing makes extensive use of hardware
acceleration in order to provide this quality even on low-end Amiga
configurations.

@{" 1.2   AmiGUS mini Key Features      " LINK features}
@{" 1.3   Hardware Overview             " LINK overview}
@{" 1.3.1 Hardware Ports                " LINK ports}
@{" 1.3.2 Hardware Components           " LINK components}
@{" 1.4   System Requirements           " LINK system}
@{" 1.4.1 Minimum Configuration         " LINK system}
@{" 1.4.2 Recommended Configuration     " LINK system}
@ENDNODE

@NODE features "Overview - AmiGUS Key Features"
@TOC contents
@{" 1     Overview                      " LINK intro}
@{" 1.1   Introduction                  " LINK intro}
@{" 1.2   AmiGUS mini Key Features      " LINK features}

  - PCMCIA bus interface for Amiga 600/1200 computers
  - 24-bit, 192 kHz stereo sample DAC
    - 1 combined analogue/optical 3.5 mm stereo output
  - 24-bit, 96 kHz stereo sample ADC
    - 1 analogue audio 3.5 mm stereo output
  - mini TOSLINK optical output, supporting 48, 96 and
    192 kHz @ 24-bit resolution
  - MP3 / OGG Vorbis hardware codec chip (VLSI VS1063)
  - Digital sound processing accelerator chip
    - 3 separate software interfaces (AHI, MHI, MIDI/Wave)
    - 32 hardware voices
      - 8 / 16-bit playback
      - Stereo panning
      - Per-voice linear sample interpolation
      - Hardware ADSR envelope
    - Full 24-bit 192 kHz processing and mixing paths
    - Hardware accelerated data transfers to / from DAC,
      ADC & MP3 chips
  - 32 MB wavetable RAM
  - LED-based VU meter, adjustable in sensitivity

@{" 1.3   Hardware Overview             " LINK overview}
@{" 1.3.1 Hardware Ports                " LINK ports}
@{" 1.3.2 Hardware Components           " LINK components}
@{" 1.4   System Requirements           " LINK system}
@{" 1.4.1 Minimum Configuration         " LINK system}
@{" 1.4.2 Recommended Configuration     " LINK system}
@ENDNODE

