@NODE components "Overview - Hardware Components"
@TOC contents
@{" 1     Overview                      " LINK intro}
@{" 1.1   Introduction                  " LINK intro}
@{" 1.2   AmiGUS mini Key Features      " LINK features}
@{" 1.3   Hardware Overview             " LINK overview}
@{" 1.3.1 Hardware Ports                " LINK ports}
@{" 1.3.2 Hardware Components           " LINK components}

+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| Component        | Function                                            |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| Digital          | The Digital Sound Processor (SHIVA) is responsible  |
| Sound            | for most of the digital sample processing and       |
| Processor        | mixing. It directly connects to the Amiga's         |
| (SHIVA)          | PCMCIA bus and provides all necessary interfaces    |
|                  | to the memory and audio support chips.              |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| 32 MB SDRAM      | This SDRAM memory chip can store up to 32 MB of     |
|                  | audio sample data for digital playback and mixing.  |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| VS1063           | The VS1063 is a hardware codec made by VLSI which   |
| Hardware Codec   | supports hardware accelerated decoding of           |
|                  | compressed audio streams such as MP3 or Ogg Vorbis. |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| PCM1808 ADC      | The PCM1808 ADC made by Texas Instruments is        |
|                  | responsible for converting all external audio       |
|                  | inputs to a 24-bit, 96 kHz digital stream which is  |
|                  | processed and mixed by the Digital Sound Processor. |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| CS4354 DAC       | The CS4354 DAC made by Cirrus Logic receives the    |
|                  | final mixed digital audio stream and converts it to |
|                  | a line-level analogue audio signal. The audio data  |
|                  | rate is always 24-bit, 192 kHz.                     |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+
| PCMCIA           | AmiGUS mini implements a PCMCIA bus interface which |
| Interface        | maps only to the I/O area, supporting 8 MB Zorro II |
|                  | Autoconfig expansions.                              |
+------------------+-----------------------------------------------------+

@{" 1.4   System Requirements           " LINK system}
@{" 1.4.1 Minimum Configuration         " LINK system}
@{" 1.4.2 Recommended Configuration     " LINK system}
